    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1472">

                <pb facs="1186" n="1070" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1070"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00.2166.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 68,
                    of July 31, 1912, transmitting correspondence relating to the revolutionary
                    attempt of General Luis Mena, of July 29, 1912.</p>
                <p>Your action in obtaining an interview with General Mena in which you communicated
                    to him President Díaz’s offer of amnesty on condition that he resign as Minister
                    of War, and in obtaining from General Mena and the General commanding the
                    Government forces letters in which they agreed to carry out such an arrangement,
                    which was afterward violated by Mena, is approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
